course: dictionary
lesson: 2877
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Doodle can mean drawing without thinking, a little drawing, a special logo, or a type of dog. Read the words around it first.
explain: Look at the phrase «doodle in the margin». The words margin and pencil tell you it means drawing little pictures while you think about something else. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have the right one.
explain: The French list of animal noises includes «cocorico (cock-a-doodle-doo)». Here doodle is part of a rooster's crow, not a drawing. The same spelling can mean very different things, so always check the sentence.
fact: Doodle as a verb means to draw little pictures or patterns without thinking much, often while doing something else.
fact: A doodle as a noun is a little drawing made like this.
fact: «Doodle on» and «doodle in the margin» are common phrases for drawing on paper while you do something else.
fact: The Google Doodle is a special logo on the Google page that changes from time to time.
fact: «Labradoodle» is a dog name, and «doodle» is a short form of it in informal talk about -doodle dogs.
exercise: What does doodle mean in «cocorico (cock-a-doodle-doo)»? | A small dog | A special logo | A little drawing | *Part of a rooster's crow
exercise: In the phrase «doodle in the margin», what does doodle mean? | To shout at someone | To run very fast | *To draw little pictures without thinking much | To sing a song loudly
exercise: What is a Google Doodle? | A type of pencil | *A special changing logo on the Google page | A map of the world | A dog breed
test: Which word tells you doodle means drawing in «doodle in the margin»? | *Margin | Loudly | Dog | Cock
test: In which sentence is doodle used as a verb? | The rooster said cock-a-doodle-doo | A doodle of a cat hung on the wall | *She doodled hearts on her spelling sheet | Her Labradoodle is very friendly
exam: Which clue tells you the meaning of doodle in «doodle in the margin»? | A dog's name | The word Google | The sound of a rooster | *The margin of the page, and drawing while you think about something else
